  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The doxology that closes the Canon, said with the Host held over the chalice — the minor elevation, so called against the elevations after each consecration. Witness do capitalises Ipsum, Ipso and Ipso; the edition prints them lowercase with witness handmissal-eo and the typical edition, adjudicated in the apparatus. EST at w009 is the only verb in the sentence and stands at its middle, at the head of its own clause, before the subjects (honor, glória) that close it. OMNIS at w018 agrees with honor alone, though the sense covers glória too.",
    "source": {
      "method": "Verified by collation against the independent witnesses below: zero substantive divergence. Accidental variants adjudicated in the apparatus.",
